Theorem TF-6c: InvokeIndirect transfer produces CONSERVATIVE

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `InvokeIndirect { dst, closure, args, normal, unwind }`
      per Annex E §AIMS TF-6c + Appendix A row 21
    - Closures have NO `MemoryContract` — same condition as TF-5a
    - CONSERVATIVE per TF-5 definition (same value)

  Soundness property:
    transfer_tf6c(InvokeIndirect { _ }) = CONSERVATIVE
      = (Owned, Unrestricted, Many, MaybeShared, Unknown, NonReusable, ALL)
    L-6 layer (b) monotonicity: f(_) = CONSERVATIVE constant function;
    trivially monotone per L-4 reflexivity.

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) CONSERVATIVE-parity with TF-5a — verify transfer_tf6c() emits
          exactly CONSERVATIVE byte-for-byte (same value as TF-5a).
      (b) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity — constant-function check identical
          to TF-5a: f(_) = CONSERVATIVE is reflexively monotone.

    Part (a) — CONSERVATIVE-parity check:
      transfer_tf6c() = CONSERVATIVE = (Owned, Unrestricted, Many,
      MaybeShared, Unknown, NonReusable, ALL = 0b111). Per Appendix A
      row 21: TF-6c emits exactly this row (identical to TF-5a row 8 +
      TF-5 row 6 + TF-6b row 20 — all four no-contract transfer rules
      converge on CONSERVATIVE). Engine verifies byte-for-byte equality
      against the canonical conservative() helper.

    Part (b) — constant-function monotonicity:
      Identical to TF-5 / TF-5a / TF-6b Part (c) — f(_) = CONSERVATIVE
      is constant on its input domain; CONSERVATIVE ≤ CONSERVATIVE by
      L-4 reflexivity on each dimension's carrier; product-order
      componentwise lift gives f(a) ≤ f(b) for any (a, b).

    Rationale for separate TF rule (per Annex E §AIMS TF-6c):
      InvokeIndirect = Invoke + closure (terminator with unwind cleanup +
      no contract). TF-6c exists to make the dispatch-via-closure-without-
      contract case explicit in the rule set. Closure handle (the
      `closure: ArcVarId` operand) generates backward demand per TF-11
      `(closure, Once)` + the args; forward transfer on `dst` is
      CONSERVATIVE because the closure body is opaque at this call site.

      All four no-contract transfer rules (TF-5, TF-5a, TF-6b, TF-6c)
      converge on CONSERVATIVE per Appendix A — the design unifies the
      no-contract output across direct/indirect x normal/unwinding axes.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) constant-function discharge per
        section_04::verify_tf6c_invokeindirect_conservative)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix A row 21 CONSERVATIVE-parity check
        per section_04::verify_tf6c_invokeindirect_conservative)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-6c emits CONSERVATIVE
        directly, no refine())

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-6c via Appendix A row 21 CONSERVATIVE-parity check + constant-function monotonicity
